# The one DeepSeek Harness generation dshline currently targets.
#
# dshline tracks Harness aggressively and supports it narrowly: one adopted
# architecture at a time, kept close to upstream master, with obsolete
# assumptions deleted rather than carried behind a compatibility layer.
#
#   revision  the exact deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness commit dshline is built
#             and validated against. The `Harness target` job in
#             .github/workflows/ci.yml checks this out, links it with
#             tools/link-harness.mjs, and blocks a merge on it.
#   version   the npm version cut from that revision. Every dsh-* dependency
#             in both manifests is pinned to it, so `pnpm install && pnpm
#             typecheck && pnpm test` on a laptop validate the same generation
#             CI does. `Harness published` boots the real consumer path
#             against it once npm carries it.
#
# Advancing this pointer IS the migration, and it is one commit: move dshline
# onto the new revision's native APIs, delete what the old one needed, run
# `node tools/harness-target.mjs --pin && pnpm install`, and edit the two
# lines below. Never advance it to a revision dshline does not already work
# against — a green `Harness target` is the claim this file makes.
#
# Upstream master is watched by the separate, non-blocking `Harness upstream`
# job. It moving is the signal to migrate, never an automatic promise of
# support.

